{
  "case_id": "2008-08-146",
  "document_hash": "bf6321e0a078bbd3677e18c3fffb09355fa31fa65d2850d97832371f61d80712",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-08-146",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf6321e0a078bbd3677e18c3fffb09355fa31fa65d2850d97832371f61d80712",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf6321e0a078-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES: M. MILLER BAKER, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioners. PAUL M. De MARCO, ESQ., Cincinnati, Ohio; on behalf of the Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Arthur Andersen LLP",
      "case_id": "2008-08-146",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf6321e0a078bbd3677e18c3fffb09355fa31fa65d2850d97832371f61d80712",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf6321e0a078-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The principal question before the Court today is whether nonparties to an arbitration agreement that are otherwise entitled to enforce that agreement under State law are foreclosed as a matter of law from seeking relief under section 3 of the Federal Arbitration Act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Wayne Carlisle et al.",
      "case_id": "2008-08-146",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf6321e0a078bbd3677e18c3fffb09355fa31fa65d2850d97832371f61d80712",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf6321e0a078-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondents' argument that section 3 forecloses such relief to nonparties is contrary to both the text of section 3 and the structure of the FAA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-08-146",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf6321e0a078bbd3677e18c3fffb09355fa31fa65d2850d97832371f61d80712",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf6321e0a078-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Before you leave the text, it says as you -- \"referable to arbitration under an agreement,\" but then it says \"shall on application of one of the parties.\" How do we know whether that is parties to the litigation or parties to the arbitration agreement?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-08-146",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf6321e0a078bbd3677e18c3fffb09355fa31fa65d2850d97832371f61d80712",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf6321e0a078-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Why do you say that section 2 -- it isn't at all clear to me that section 2 says State law determines whether somebody not a party to the arbitration agreement can -- can enforce it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-08-146",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf6321e0a078bbd3677e18c3fffb09355fa31fa65d2850d97832371f61d80712",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf6321e0a078-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: May -- may I ask you this? Let's assume State law said we -- we don't recognize stays at this stage of the game. Therefore, we will not give a stay to anyone. Would State law prevail?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Baker",
      "case_id": "2008-08-146",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf6321e0a078bbd3677e18c3fffb09355fa31fa65d2850d97832371f61d80712",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf6321e0a078-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The mere request for relief under section 3 and the denial of that request triggers appellate jurisdiction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-08-146",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf6321e0a078bbd3677e18c3fffb09355fa31fa65d2850d97832371f61d80712",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf6321e0a078-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What are the instances in which somebody who is not a signatory might seem to have a right to enforce it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Baker",
      "case_id": "2008-08-146",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf6321e0a078bbd3677e18c3fffb09355fa31fa65d2850d97832371f61d80712",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf6321e0a078-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There's assignment, successor in interest, assumption, estoppel."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. De Marco",
      "case_id": "2008-08-146",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf6321e0a078bbd3677e18c3fffb09355fa31fa65d2850d97832371f61d80712",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf6321e0a078-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Estoppel is what you invoke when you have no contract to invoke, and this version of equitable estoppel is what you invoke when you have no arbitration agreement to invoke."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-08-146",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf6321e0a078bbd3677e18c3fffb09355fa31fa65d2850d97832371f61d80712",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf6321e0a078-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What is the criterion for identifying a section 3 stay?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-08-146",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf6321e0a078bbd3677e18c3fffb09355fa31fa65d2850d97832371f61d80712",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf6321e0a078-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What do you do with third party beneficiary assignment assumption?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. De Marco",
      "case_id": "2008-08-146",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf6321e0a078bbd3677e18c3fffb09355fa31fa65d2850d97832371f61d80712",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf6321e0a078-0001-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All of those examples, Justice Kennedy, in all of those examples the right to enforce the agreement, let's say the right to procure a stay based on the agreement, flows from the intention of the parties to the original agreement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-08-146",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf6321e0a078bbd3677e18c3fffb09355fa31fa65d2850d97832371f61d80712",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf6321e0a078-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Mr. De Marco, can I ask you this question? In section 3 do you agree with his reading of the word \"parties,\" or do you think \"parties\" just means parties to the contract?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-08-146",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf6321e0a078bbd3677e18c3fffb09355fa31fa65d2850d97832371f61d80712",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf6321e0a078-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: You are concerned about -- does that mean you agree with him that \"parties\" means parties to the action and not parties to the contract?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-08-146",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf6321e0a078bbd3677e18c3fffb09355fa31fa65d2850d97832371f61d80712",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf6321e0a078-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: What would you think about saying that some parties -- some parties to the case who are not parties to the contract can as third parties, nonetheless, enforce arbitration?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-08-146",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf6321e0a078bbd3677e18c3fffb09355fa31fa65d2850d97832371f61d80712",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf6321e0a078-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: If the \"parties\" in -- in section 3 means parties to the arbitration agreement, would that mean that a -- someone who is not a party to the litigation could file a stay motion under section 3, someone who is not a party to the litigation but is a party to the arbitration agreement?"
    },
    {
